# Frontend — restrictive rules

Source of truth: `CLAUDE.md`. If a decision here conflicts with Trello "Not MPV", the board wins — update `CLAUDE.md`.

## Structure (mandatory)

- Feature-based: domain code lives in `frontend/src/features/<domain>/{components,hooks,types,utils}`.
- Thin pages in `frontend/src/pages/`: they wire hooks + components. **Forbidden** to bury fetch, mutations, or heavy business logic in the page.
- Shell only in `frontend/src/app/{layout,router,providers}`.
- Cross-feature code only under `frontend/src/shared/{components,hooks,services,utils,types,store,config}` with a barrel `index.ts` when that pattern already exists.
- Domain constant maps (labels/colors/icons, not functions): flat file under `shared/` (e.g. `orderStatus.constants.ts`), **not** through a barrel — same idea as backend `defaultTags.ts`.
- Alias `@/*` → `src/*`. Do not use long relative imports across features.
- `inbox` / `communication` are empty scaffolds (Not MPV). **Do not** build the unified inbox, ChannelAdapter, or conversation UI.

## Exports and routing

- `pages/*`: **only** `export default function XPage()`.
- Everything else (components, hooks, utils, services): **only** named exports.
- New page = one `lazyPage(() => import('@/pages/XPage'))` entry in `app/router/index.tsx`. No lazy entry = incomplete.

## UI and design system

- Prefer `frontend/src/shared/components` first (`SincraButton`, `Input`, `Select`, `SincraModal`, `ConfirmDeleteModal`, `Table`, `Tabs`, `Drawer`, `EmptyState`, `KpiCardsRow`, `DateRangeFilter`, etc.).
- **Forbidden** to invent a parallel button/modal/input when shared already has one.
- Colors and typography: tokens from `frontend/src/index.css` (`bg-primary`, `text-ink-muted`, `text-error`, …). **No** ad-hoc hex in Tailwind except documented exceptions (ECharts canvas cannot resolve CSS vars → hex allowed only there).
- Icons: `lucide-react` (except AI agent avatars = PNGs in `public/`).
- UI copy in **Spanish**. User-facing text: no "OAuth", no internal API names unless that screen already does.
- Desktop-first. No mobile-first redesigns. Acceptable minimum: horizontal scroll on tables. Sidebar is already `max-md:hidden` — do not turn it into a drawer unless explicitly asked.
- Do not switch basemap to CARTO (API KEY watermark). Keep OpenStreetMap + current Leaflet patterns (`divIcon`, `isolate`, `clients-map.css`).

## State and data

- Remote state: **TanStack Query** in feature hooks (`useClients`, `useSaveOrder`, …). Stable hierarchical query keys (`['clients']`, `['clients','map',filters]`, `['orders', id]`).
- Mutations: invalidate via feature helpers (`invalidateClientQueries`, `invalidateOrderQueries`). Do not blindly invalidate the whole tree.
- Shared `channel` / `dateFrom` / `dateTo` across Map/Stats/Orders: **only** `shared/store/filtersStore` (Zustand). Page-local filters (search, status, page, granularity) stay local.
- Tests that touch the store: `useFiltersStore.getState().clearFilters()` in `beforeEach`.
- HTTP: **only** `api` from `@/shared/services` (`credentials: 'include'`). No bare `fetch` to the API.
- Notifications: `notifySuccess` / `notifyError` / `notifyWithUndo` from shared. No ad-hoc toasts.
- Auth/session: httpOnly cookies via backend; never store JWT in `localStorage`.

## Feature ownership

- Client and Order stay separate on purpose. Notes/Tags tabs may be near-copies; **do not** abstract a mega ClientOrOrderNotes component without an explicit decision.
- Reuse shared when the pattern is already cross-cutting (`NotesTab`, `DateRangeFilter`, `ConfirmDeleteModal`).
- Map: Clients/Orders layer toggle is **binary** (no "Both"). Colors: clients `primary`, orders `primary-dark`. `approximate` = no written address.

## React / TypeScript (repo practices)

- Names in **English**, descriptive. `catch (error)`, never `catch (e)`. Callbacks: `(client) => …`, not `(c) => …`.
- Explicit typing for props, API data, and generics (`useState<Set<string>>(new Set())`).
- `setState(prev => …)` when the next value depends on the previous one.
- `useMemo` only when the cost is real (expensive derived lists, table columns, KPIs). Not by default.
- Small components. If a page/component mixes fetch + UI + navigation + modals, extract hooks/subcomponents **before** it grows further.
- Accessibility on interactives: keyboard, focus, `aria-*` on loading buttons (`aria-busy`), decorative icons `aria-hidden`.
- Forms: follow existing patterns (react-hook-form where already used; validate email with shared `EMAIL_PATTERN` when applicable).

## Tests

- Vitest + Testing Library. **Given/When/Then** comments above `it(...)`, matching the rest of the repo.
- Co-locate `*.test.ts(x)` next to the file.
- Mock `api` / ECharts (`vi.mock`) when jsdom cannot run the real runtime.
- After feature changes: `cd frontend && npm test` (or the touched file) and `npm run lint` before calling it done.

## Forbidden scope (Not MPV)

Do not implement: unified inbox, WhatsApp/Instagram/Messenger adapters, interactive Automations (4-agent toggles), real Stripe paywall, real active sessions, real notification delivery. The AI Agents page is **static/informational** (Sincra/Sincro; no Hermes in the UI).
